WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.850
Even if our ancestors
consumed a full spectrum

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.450
of vitamins and minerals every day,

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.160
mouths would very likely
still grow too small.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.320
What was true for our ancestors

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.310
was also true for us,

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:17.520
because the problem had less
to do with what we were eating

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.010
than how we ate it, chewing.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.640
It was the constant stress of chewing

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.490
that was lacking from our diets,

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:28.760
not specifically vitamins A, B, C, or D.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.760
95% of the industrialized diet was soft.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.400
Our ancient ancestors chewed
for hours a day, every day.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.240
Because they chewed so much,
their mouths, their teeth,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.680
their throats, and their faces

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.910
grew to be wide and strong and pronounced.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.730
This larger mouth with straighter teeth

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.220
allowed them to breathe more easily.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.800
Food in industrialized
societies was so processed

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.870
that it hardly required
any chewing at all.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.300
Here's some of the industrialized mush

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.780
that I grew up eating.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.960
Yes, of course I had extractions.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.510
Yes, of course I needed
braces and headgear

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:06.700
and everything else.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.160
Here's the typical modern
American diet today.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.770
Cheese sauces, baked goods,
spaghetti, fried roots.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.130
It's all soft.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:19.780
Even what's considered healthy
foods, smoothies, yogurt,

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.470
avocados, oatmeal, it's all soft.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.420
Healthy chewing starts in infancy.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.970
The chewing and sucking stress
required for breastfeeding

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:33.480
exercises the masseter
and other facial muscles,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.850
and stimulates more bone growth,

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.600
allowing for that upper palate to drop,

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.000
which leads to wider airways.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.550
Until a few hundred years ago,

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:46.180
mothers would breastfeed
infants up to two to four years,

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.030
sometimes even longer.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.480
The more time infants
spent chewing and sucking,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.510
the more they'd increase their
chances of breathing better

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.520
later on in life.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:00.010
With industrialization came
bottle-feeding and baby formula.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.710
Soon, in many societies,

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.240
infants were hardly breastfed at all.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.250
Now, dozens and dozens of studies

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.910
in the past two decades
have supported this claim.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.380
They've shown lower incidence
of snoring and sleep apnea

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.710
in infants who are breastfed longer

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.930
versus those who are bottle-fed.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.970
This is why so many of the
skulls that I've examined

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:23.040
in the Museum of Archeology
and Anthropology,

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.460
that I'd seen at the Paris quarries,

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:28.990
this is why they had narrow
faces and crooked teeth.

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:32.020
It's one of the main reasons
why so many of us today

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.940
are chronically stuffed-up,

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.990
why our airways are
clogged, why we need sprays

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.890
and pills and surgery,

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:41.741
just to get a fresh breath of air.

00:02:41.741 --> 00:02:44.393
 

